.TH "bead recurrence materialize" 1  "bead recurrence materialize " 
.SH NAME
bead recurrence materialize \- Materialize the next occurrence from a template
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead recurrence materialize\fR <\fB\-\-id\fR> [\fB\-\-actor\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create the next occurrence in the recurrence series as a new issue.
Each occurrence carries a stable series reference and the created issue ID.
.PP
This is an explicit operation \- bead\-rs never automatically creates occurrences on schedules.
External schedulers should call this command when they want a new occurrence created.
.PP
EXAMPLES:
  bead recurrence materialize \-\-id template\-001
  bead recurrence materialize \-\-id daily\-review \-\-actor scheduler\-1
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR=\fIID\fR
Template ID
.TP
\fB\-\-actor\fR=\fIACTOR\fR
Actor performing the materialization
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
